R-SC3 R-AD35 R-AD2 R-RG4 R-RG5 R-AP1 R-DI14 R-T10 R-IX3 R-CM16 (slice 206f): `tln tool install acme/foo` with a registry (entry `commands`). The home, the fakes and the build are run 1 of tool/ti1-install: the same 4 releases, the same bundle fetch, the same build, the same output. The registry is in config.toml (`registry`), TALON_GITHUB_API is set (no token source: no `programs gh`).
The only change: the release list is the registry list (R-SC3). The calls are the guard (R-RG4: the kept answer, `GET /repos/acme/foo`, a write), then R-AP1 (`GET /v1/packages/acme/foo/releases`, the copy) instead of the 3 calls of the GitHub list. R-AP1 answers 200, so no GitHub release list, no `programs curl` for an ingest, no ingest (R-AD35 starts at a 404). The bundle is fetched and its header read as in `direct` (R-T10): the registry has no kind of an app bundle in this answer.
Reading (D1): `ToolFlow` calls `FullName.read!` where it called `Github.releases!`, and turns the answer into the same candidates (`Index.Candidate`).
Q547 (round 2): the expected calls.log has no `POST /v1/closure` and no queue call: `tool install` and `x` send neither a closure query nor the share queue in 206f.
